values ('f1a2b3c4-6d7e-4f51-8a01-1b2c3d4e5f11', 'child-welfare', 'Child Welfare', 'Understand why child welfare exists, how it developed, and how its values, laws, and policy tensions shape practice. Use developmental and ecological knowledge to interpret safety, trauma, and protective capacity; map interprofessional systems; and recognize maltreatment without simplistic assumptions about poverty, culture, disability, and family stress. Practice reporting, safety assessment, documentation, family engagement, prevention, placement, and permanency work, and connect courts, evidence-based intervention, equity, tribal sovereignty, transition-age youth supports, and ethical, data-informed reform.');

